+## Task 9 superseding amendment: Global DSP + shared Linked Lock
+
+Before completing Task 9, apply the approved user requirement that **Global DSP** is the primary user mode over the existing session-zero `DynamicsProcessing` branch. It is one shared preference shown in Simple and Advanced, defaults ON, and becomes active only after the existing bounded `DspScopeProbe` verifies the current route. Successful effect construction alone remains unverified. While verified Global DSP is active, ordinary positive/negative normalization uses DSP gain/limiter without routine Samsung Media writes; hard Media safety remains independent. If proof/capability is lost, neutralize DSP before fallback.
+
+Global DSP processes an indivisible mix, so per-app/system exclusions that cannot be honestly enforced remain visible but disabled/dimmed only while `VERIFIED_GLOBAL_MIX` is actually active. Preference ON with unavailable DSP must show compatible fallback and leave selective controls usable.
+
+**Default Linked Lock is also shared across both views.** With the lock ON, Minimum/Maximum Output Ceiling controls stay visible but disabled/dimmed in Simple and Advanced; with it OFF they unlock in place without value jumps and preserve `lower <= upper`. Global DSP and Linked Lock are independent switches and all four combinations are valid.
